Package: CooccurrenceAnalysis
Title: Domain-Neutral Co-Occurrence Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Brian", "Chapman", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Domain-neutral analysis of co-occurrence in binary
    (presence/absence) event data, where records accumulate events that each
    carry one item. Provides pairwise association statistics (one-sided
    Fisher exact or Pearson chi-square tests, with Benjamini-Hochberg,
    Bonferroni or Holm correction), significance-filtered co-occurrence
    networks with Leiden or Louvain communities from 'igraph' and per-node
    metrics, group-stratified networks, a hierarchical Dirichlet process
    Bernoulli mixture fit jointly across groups by approximate
    coordinate-ascent variational inference, frequent itemsets and
    association rules enumerated by 'arules', and 'ggplot2' plots. Every
    method is published by others; the package began as a port of the
    Julia 'CooccurrenceAnalysis' package and carries no domain vocabulary.
